From: klaus.goger@theobroma-systems.com (Klaus Goger)
Date: Fri, 15 Dec 2017 12:44:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] arm64: dts: rockchip: use SPDX-License-Identifier
In-Reply-To: <20171215114427.32059-1-klaus.goger@theobroma-systems.com>
References: <20171215114427.32059-1-klaus.goger@theobroma-systems.com>
Message-ID: <20171215114427.32059-2-klaus.goger@theobroma-systems.com>
To: linux-arm-kernel@lists.infradead.org
List-Id: linux-arm-kernel.lists.infradead.org

Update all 64bit rockchip devicetree files to use SPDX-License-Identifiers.

All devicetrees claim to be either GPL or X11 while the actual license
text is MIT. Therefore we use MIT for the SPDX tag as X11 is clearly
wrong.

Signed-off-by: Klaus Goger <klaus.goger@theobroma-systems.com>
---

